lease-date uncertainty as a ledger-calendar caveat rather than a resolved fact.\"}],\"optionalSuggestions\":[\"Add the 2024 U.S. ACS 1-year same-table value to historicalContext and demote California to an external benchmark.\",\"Make the downside tail more concrete by quantifying what prior-year stagnation or subsidy-related churn would imply for the percentage point change.\",\"Check that all JSON fields continue to use percent units and one-decimal rounding after revising the prior and interval.\"]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-39-25z-census-acs-broadband-subscription-65-plus-share-2025/draft_command.json:11:    \"/Users/maxghenis/_worktrees/brier-aging-wave2/records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-39-25z-census-acs-broadband-subscription-65-plus-share-2025/draft_codex_last_message.txt\",\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-39-25z-census-acs-broadband-subscription-65-plus-share-2025/revision_prompt.md:17:- catalogSlug: \"broadband-subscription-65-plus-2025\"\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-39-25z-census-acs-broadband-subscription-65-plus-share-2025/revision_prompt.md:124:{\"slug\":\"broadband-subscription-65-plus-2025\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"ACS 65+ Broadband Subscription Share, 2025\",\"question\":\"U.S. Census Bureau American Community Survey 2025 ACS 1-Year Estimates Detailed Table B28005, population 65 years and over in households with a computer and a broadband Internet subscription divided by total population 65 years and over in households, first print, percent.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":86.0,\"ciLow\":83.4,\"ciHigh\":88.6,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-09-10\",\"resolutionSource\":\"U.S. Census Bureau American Community Survey 1-Year Estimates Detailed Table B28005\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2025.B28005?q=B28005\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to 100 * B28005_017E / B28005_014E for geography United States in the first public 2025 ACS 1-Year Estimates Detailed Table B28005 print, rounded to one decimal percentage point. Use the original Census first-posted estimate and ignore later revisions or corrections unless Census replaces the first public file before the public release completes.\",\"dataPointId\":\"census.acs.broadband_subscription_65_plus.share.2025.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"2023 ACS 5-year B28005 65+ broadband share\",\"value\":82.6},{\"label\":\"2024 ACS 1-year California B28005 65+ broadband share\",\"value\":91.4},{\"label\":\"latest ACS 5-year households with broadband subscription\",\"value\":91.0},{\"label\":\"latest ACS 5-year population 65+ with no computer in household\",\"value\":8.7}],\"drivers\":[\"Aging-cohort replacement raises 65+ internet adoption\",\"Broadband subscription definition includes cellular data, satellite, fixed wireless, and other non-dial-up service\",\"Gains should slow as the remaining offline 65+ population is more selected\",\"ACS sampling and weighting noise can move a one-year national age subgroup by more than one percentage point\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2025.B28005?q=B28005\",\"https://api.census.gov/data/2024/acs/acs1/groups/B28005.html\",\"https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT5Y2023.B28005?g=040XX00US16%240500000_010XX00US&q=ages+with+broadband+access\",\"https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2024.B28005?g=040XX00US06&q=Telephone%2C+Computer%2C+and+Internet+Access\",\"https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/data/summary-file.2024.html\",\"https://www.census.gov/data/what-is-data-census-gov/upcoming-releases.html\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-07-21T01:39:34Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for 2025 ACS 65+ Broadband Subscription Share\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Framing and exact resolver: the target is Census ACS Detailed Table B28005, universe population in households, United States, 2025 ACS 1-year first print. The numerator is B28005_017E, 65 years and over, has a computer, with a broadband Internet subscription; the denominator is B28005_014E, total 65 years and over. The resolution source URL is the exact data.census.gov table page for ACSDT1Y2025.B28005.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspect Census API variable metadata for 2024 ACS 1-year B28005\",\"result\":\"Fetched variable definitions: B28005 has 78 variables; B28005_014E is total 65 years and over; B28005_017E is 65 years and over with a computer and a broadband Internet subscription; B28005_001E is the total table population count.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspect Census data.census.gov 2023 ACS 5-year B28005 United States row as reference-class anchor\",\"result\":\"Fetched United States 2023 ACS 5-year B28005 counts: total population in households 324,275,237; 65 years and over total 54,267,407; 65+ with broadband subscription 44,841,576; computed share 44,841,576 / 54,267,407 * 100 = 82.6 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspect Census data.census.gov 2024 ACS 1-year B28005 California row for latest same-table high-adoption benchmark\",\"result\":\"Fetched California 2024 ACS 1-year B28005 counts: total population in households 38,537,958; 65 years and over total 6,333,225; 65+ with broadband subscription 5,786,620; computed share 5,786,620 / 6,333,225 * 100 = 91.4 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspect Census ACS computer-and-internet use official results page for latest ACS summary measures\",\"result\":\"Fetched latest ACS summary measures for the United States: households with a computer 95.5 percent; households with a broadband Internet subscription 91.0 percent; population 65+ with no computer in household 8.7 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspect Census ACS summary-file and release-calendar pages for release mechanics\",\"result\":\"Fetched Census summary-file metadata: 2024 ACS 1-year summary file table B28005 file acsdt1y2024-b28005.dat was listed with timestamp 2025-09-11 09:00 and size 1.3M; Census upcoming releases page was last revised July 20, 2026 and listed September 2026 entries including 9/10/2026 and 9/24/2026. I found no separate 2025 ACS 1-year schedule page in the indexed official pages, so the chosen 2026-09-10 date should be treated as tied to the expected ACS 1-year September first-release slot and rechecked against any later Census ACS schedule notice.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base rate/reference class: recent ACS computer-and-internet measures show most U.S. households already have broadband, but the 65+ population remains below the all-household average because disability, fixed-income, rurality, and cohort effects are concentrated among older adults. The 2023 ACS 5-year same-table United States benchmark was 82.6 percent, while 2024 California was 91.4 percent, so a 2025 U.S. 1-year value in the mid-80s is a conservative national anchor rather than a California-style upper benchmark.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, one-off, and mechanism: level starts from the low-to-mid 80s for the national 65+ B28005 share. Momentum is positive because each entering 65-year-old cohort is more connected than the oldest cohorts leaving the population, and the broadband category includes cellular data plans. One-off BEAD deployment effects are limited by timing because many funded projects will not materially change 2025 ACS collection-year subscriptions. Policy support such as ACP had ended before 2025, creating some affordability drag for low-income older households.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: persistence prior is 2024 national 65+ broadband share estimated at 84.5 from the 2023 ACS 5-year United States B28005 share of 82.6, current all-household broadband 91.0, 65+ no-computer 8.7, and 2024 California 65+ same-table share 91.4. Historical sample uses recent same-concept annualized changes of roughly +2.3, +2.1, and +1.6 percentage points, giving sigma = sqrt((2.3^2 + 2.1^2 + 1.6^2) / 3) = 2.0 percentage points. Mechanism update adds +1.5 points for cohort replacement and continued mobile/fixed-wireless subscription diffusion, minus 0.0 to 0.3 for affordability drag, yielding point 86.0. The 80% half-width is about 1.28*sigma = 1.28*2.0 = 2.6, so bounds are 86.0 - 2.6 = 83.4 and 86.0 + 2.6 = 88.6.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-considerations: upside risk is a stronger-than-expected jump in cellular-data-plan reporting or older-adult smartphone adoption, which would land above the interval if the 2025 share exceeds 88.6 percent. Downside risk is affordability churn after subsidy expiration, survey-composition noise, or a stall among the oldest and lowest-income households, which would land below the interval if the first print is under 83.4 percent. An outside the interval result would most likely reflect either a definitional/table change or a large one-year ACS sampling/weighting move rather than ordinary trend continuation.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":86.0,\"ciLow\":83.4,\"ciHigh\":88.6}]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-39-25z-census-acs-broadband-subscription-65-plus-share-2025/revision_prompt.md:127:{\"summary\":\"The target contract is mostly coherent, but the draft relies on an estimated 2024 prior and unstated annual-change sample when exact same-series ACS 1-year history should be available.\",\"requiredFixes\":[{\"rubricItem\":\"model_prior\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"summary\":\"The draft uses a constructed 2024 national prior and California/5-year proxies instead of citing the same-series U.S. ACS 1-year B28005 history available before resolution.\",\"actionRequested\":\"Fetch and state the latest available U.S. ACS 1-year B28005_017E/B28005_014E values, preferably a short 2021-2024 same-series history, or explicitly explain why those exact annu